{"name":"Bonsai Tint","hex":"#c5d1b2","fetched":"2026-10-11","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"bonsai","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A tree or plant that has been miniaturized by planting it in a small pot, restricting its roots, and by careful pruning.","The art of planting and growing trees or plants in such a manner."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To make into a bonsai by restricting the roots and pruning."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/bonsai"},{"term":"tint","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A slight coloring.","A pale or faint tinge of any color; especially, a variation of a color obtained by adding white (contrast shade)"]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To shade, to color."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/tint"}],"entries":[{"title":"Bonsai","blocks":[{"text":"Bonsai is the Japanese art of growing and shaping miniature trees in containers, with a long documented history of influences and native Japanese development over a thousand years, and with unique aesthetics, cultural history, and terminology derived from its evolution in Japan. Similar arts exist in other cultures, including Korea's bunjae, the Chinese art of penjing, and the miniature living landscapes of Vietnamese Hòn non bộ."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/94/Bonsai%2C_Kenshin_Toge.jpg/330px-Bonsai%2C_Kenshin_Toge.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Bonsai","wikidata":"Q64365"},{"title":"Tint, shade and tone","blocks":[{"text":"In color theory, a tint is a mixture of a color with white, which increases lightness, while a shade is a mixture with black, which increases darkness. A tone is produced either by mixing a color with gray, or by both tinting and shading. Mixing a color with any neutral color reduces the chroma, or colorfulness, while the perceived hue can be affected slightly."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/d6/Tint-tone-shade.svg/330px-Tint-tone-shade.svg.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Tint%2C_shade_and_tone","wikidata":"Q2749750"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/66/Bonsai_tree2.jpg/500px-Bonsai_tree2.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/66/Bonsai_tree2.jpg/1280px-Bonsai_tree2.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/66/Bonsai_tree2.jpg/500px-Bonsai_tree2.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Bonsai at the Omiya Bonsai Art Museum","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ABonsai_tree2.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/4b/Eurya%2C_1970-2007.jpg/500px-Eurya%2C_1970-2007.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/4b/Eurya%2C_1970-2007.jpg/1280px-Eurya%2C_1970-2007.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/4b/Eurya%2C_1970-2007.jpg/500px-Eurya%2C_1970-2007.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Bonsai at the National Bonsai & Penjing Museum at the United States National Arboretum","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AEurya%2C_1970-2007.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/49/Bonsai%2C_%22Sandai_Shogun%22.jpg/500px-Bonsai%2C_%22Sandai_Shogun%22.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/49/Bonsai%2C_%22Sandai_Shogun%22.jpg/500px-Bonsai%2C_%22Sandai_Shogun%22.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_c